    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "With 11 untapped lands and Rites of Flourishing on the battlefield (allowing an extra land drop), KimiK2 should play Overflowing Basin first before casting Jolly Gerbils. Playing the land first ensures they don't miss the extra land drop if they cast a spell first and forget, and more importantly, they should consider whether Ghirapur Orrery (4 mana) is a better play than Jolly Gerbils. However, the main sequencing issue is casting a creature before playing a land - they should play Overflowing Basin first, then decide on their spell. Additionally, Jolly Gerbils' draw trigger requires 'giving a gift' which is a specific mechanic from Bloomburrow - only Perch Protection in hand has a gift ability. The Gerbils as a 2/3 for 2 mana is fine but provides minimal board impact compared to Ghirapur Orrery which would provide card advantage and extra land drops for a player who has 8 lands on board.",
