    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Gem3F Spike has Fist of Suns on the battlefield, which allows paying {W}{U}{B}{R}{G} instead of a spell's mana cost. Atarka, World Render normally costs {5}{R}{G} (7 mana). Looking at available lands: Forest (G), Crucible of the Spirit Dragon, Island (U), Mystic Monastery (W/U/R), Fist of Suns (already paid for), Swamp (B). The Crucible has storage counters that can produce any color for Dragon spells. With Crucible's stored counters, they could potentially produce the {W}{U}{B}{R}{G} for 5 mana total instead of 7 mana for the normal cost. Even without stored counters, Crucible can tap for colorless. The player has 8 lands/mana sources but several are tapped or produce wrong colors for {5}{R}{G}. Actually, looking more carefully at the board - all lands appear untapped for Gem3F Spike (Forest, Crucible, Island, Mystic Monastery, Swamp, plus Fist of Suns). That's Forest(G), Crucible(C or colored for dragons), Island(U), Mystic Monastery(W/U/R), Swamp(B) = 5 lands. For {W}{U}{B}{R}{G}: Mystic Monastery→W, Island→U, Swamp→B, Crucible (remove counter)→R, Forest→G. This costs exactly 5 mana and leaves nothing extra. For {5}{R}{G}: they need 7 mana total including R and G, but they only have 5 lands producing at most 5-6 mana (Crucible with counters). They likely can't even cast it for {5}{R}{G} without the Crucible counters anyway. Using the alternative cost of {W}{U}{B}{R}{G} saves 2 mana, which could matter for holding up interaction or playing the Island from hand. Declining the Fist of Suns alternative cost wastes 2 mana worth of value.",
