      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Sunscorch Regent is a significant flying threat that grows larger and gains life for its controller with every spell cast. A 1/1 Saproling Token is nearly irrelevant. Fighting the token wastes the fight trigger on a meaningless target while leaving the real threat on the board.",
      "action_taken": "Chose to fight the Saproling Token instead of Sunscorch Regent",
      "better_line": "Fight the Sunscorch Regent to remove the growing flying threat",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 380,
      "player": "Gem3F Spike",
      "decision_index": 358,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Discarded Sol Ring claiming they already had one in play, but their battlefield shows Arcane Signet, not Sol Ring. Sol Ring is arguably the best card in Commander (1 mana for 2 colorless every turn) and would significantly accelerate their remaining expensive spells like Nissa's Renewal (6 mana) and Acidic Slime (5 mana).",
      "action_taken": "Discarded Sol Ring based on the incorrect belief it was already in play.",
      "better_line": "Discard Scaretiller or Seer's Sundial instead - both are less impactful than Sol Ring's persistent mana advantage. Scaretiller is a slow 1/4 body and Seer's Sundial requires additional mana investment per landfall trigger.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 395,
      "player": "Kimi25 ESPN",
      "decision_index": 368,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Flooded Grove was tapped for just {C} when it could have produced two mana ({G}{G}, {G}{U}, or {U}{U}) by paying the {G/U} hybrid activation cost with another available land. This wastes the land's mana-doubling potential, effectively losing 1 mana.",
      "action_taken": "Activated Flooded Grove for {C} (1 colorless mana)",
      "better_line": "Use another untapped green or blue source to pay the {G/U} hybrid cost and activate Flooded Grove for {G}{G}, {G}{U}, or {U}{U} (2 mana total), netting an extra mana",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 399,
      "player": "KimiK2 Sarge",
      "decision_index": 375,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Cast Kwain before playing available land drops (Thriving Grove and Island in hand, with Rites of Flourishing allowing an extra land). While 8 mana sources were already sufficient to cast Kwain and equip Boots, playing lands first is strictly better sequencing - it maximizes available mana and could matter for future plays this turn.",
      "action_taken": "Chose to cast Kwain, Itinerant Meddler before playing lands",
      "better_line": "Play Thriving Grove and Island first (two land drops available thanks to Rites of Flourishing), then cast Kwain and equip Swiftfoot Boots with remaining mana.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 434,
      "player": "KimiK2 Sarge",
      "decision_index": 403,
    }
  ],
